00:28:09.160 --> 00:28:12.720
we have dates that people cannot travel.

00:28:11.280 --> 00:28:14.760
As you become an owner, you'll see you

00:28:12.720 --> 00:28:16.680
have to have this in business because

00:28:14.760 --> 00:28:18.600
you have surges in business. Not every

00:28:16.680 --> 00:28:20.320
month is the same. And so, sometimes you

00:28:18.600 --> 00:28:22.160
just got to be there even when you got a

00:28:20.320 --> 00:28:23.600
wedding that you'd rather go to. So,

00:28:22.160 --> 00:28:25.760
what do you need to do? You need to give

00:28:23.600 --> 00:28:28.280
clear feedback and a real chance to say,

00:28:25.760 --> 00:28:30.120
"Hey, during this time, you actually

00:28:28.280 --> 00:28:31.720
can't travel." And I know we're buddies

00:28:30.120 --> 00:28:32.840
and I know you're an adult and I hate to

00:28:31.720 --> 00:28:34.520
tell you you can't go do anything in

00:28:32.840 --> 00:28:36.440
life. That feels weird to me. But if I

00:28:34.520 --> 00:28:38.280
give you this opportunity off, what

00:28:36.440 --> 00:28:40.200
about everybody else? And And you can

00:28:38.280 --> 00:28:41.160
always negotiate. You can say, "Listen,

00:28:40.200 --> 00:28:43.080
I'm going to need you to work two

00:28:41.160 --> 00:28:44.880
Saturdays to make up for it." And then I

00:28:43.080 --> 00:28:47.254
can say he's done double the work to

00:28:44.880 --> 00:28:49.000
cover that one spot. Ready, go. Because

00:28:47.254 --> 00:28:50.520
[music] floor three is getting that

00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:52.600
right people to the right elevator,

00:28:50.520 --> 00:28:54.280
right? But remember floor four gives

00:28:52.600 --> 00:28:55.680
them that reason to keep climbing. And

00:28:54.280 --> 00:28:57.920
then the penthouse is where you build a

00:28:55.680 --> 00:28:59.200
system that actually climbs with you.

00:28:57.920 --> 00:29:00.920
The penthouse sets the tone for

00:28:59.200 --> 00:29:04.120
everything. So this is where owners and

00:29:00.920 --> 00:29:06.200
CEOs operate. And the job looks nothing

00:29:04.120 --> 00:29:08.920
like the work that got you here. You are

00:29:06.200 --> 00:29:10.360
not paid as a CEO to do tasks. You

00:29:08.920 --> 00:29:12.160
aren't even usually the one giving

00:29:10.360 --> 00:29:14.280
instructions to most of the team. Your

00:29:12.160 --> 00:29:16.400
main job now is to set the tone for the

00:29:14.280 --> 00:29:18.000
whole business. Because everyone below

00:29:16.400 --> 00:29:19.400
you is watching you to decide how

00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:21.360
seriously [music] to take the mission.

00:29:19.400 --> 00:29:23.320
So at the penthouse, I really think you

00:29:21.360 --> 00:29:25.920
lead through three pillars. And those

00:29:23.320 --> 00:29:27.600
three pillars are what you decide, where

00:29:25.920 --> 00:29:30.000
you point, and what you model. [music]

00:29:27.600 --> 00:29:33.160
So the foundation for your business, it

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:34.880
starts with judgment. So this is

00:29:33.160 --> 00:29:37.560
what your decisions are. [music]

00:29:34.880 --> 00:29:39.480
Firstly, there is one thing you must

00:29:37.560 --> 00:29:41.600
stop doing here. And that's making a

00:29:39.480 --> 00:29:43.520
thousand decisions a day. It feels

00:29:41.600 --> 00:29:46.080
productive, but it quietly drags you

00:29:43.520 --> 00:29:47.560
down. So your value at the top is

00:29:46.080 --> 00:29:49.600
getting the few decisions that matter

00:29:47.560 --> 00:29:52.520
right, and then building people who can

00:29:49.600 --> 00:29:54.200
handle the rest. Your next job is really

00:29:52.520 --> 00:29:56.400
vision. So the most valuable thing you

00:29:54.200 --> 00:29:58.000
can build clarity around is [music]

00:29:56.400 --> 00:29:59.800
where you're going.

00:29:58.000 --> 00:30:01.480
And then repeat it until every person

00:29:59.800 --> 00:30:04.720
can say it back to you. If you have a

00:30:01.480 --> 00:30:06.160
vision on a wall, but nobody's repeating

00:30:04.720 --> 00:30:08.120
it or engraving it in their daily

00:30:06.160 --> 00:30:09.880
conversations, then you don't actually

00:30:08.120 --> 00:30:11.960
have a real vision. You have to carry

00:30:09.880 --> 00:30:14.240
yourself in every part of your life, and

00:30:11.960 --> 00:30:15.680
every part of your company as the same

00:30:14.240 --> 00:30:16.960
part of the vision. And it's so

00:30:15.680 --> 00:30:18.520
important that we even have it on the

00:30:16.960 --> 00:30:19.960
walls, and I'm constantly reminding

00:30:18.520 --> 00:30:21.920
people to look at them. Lastly, of

00:30:19.960 --> 00:30:23.520
consistency. One of my favorite lines,

00:30:21.920 --> 00:30:25.000
and also least favorite lines of all

00:30:23.520 --> 00:30:26.600
time cuz it's so annoying when it gets

00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:28.360
rubbed in your face, is how you do

00:30:26.600 --> 00:30:30.640
anything is how you do everything. If

00:30:28.360 --> 00:30:32.440
you speak carelessly, can't hold a clear

00:30:30.640 --> 00:30:34.560
thought, or don't look after yourself or

00:30:32.440 --> 00:30:36.320
your word, people quietly wonder whether

00:30:34.560 --> 00:30:38.000
to put their careers behind you. They

00:30:36.320 --> 00:30:40.600
read the small things as evidence of the

00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:42.480
big ones. And the biggest one is this:

00:30:40.600 --> 00:30:43.960
Do what you say you're going to do. So

00:30:42.480 --> 00:30:45.760
everything you do at this level, I

00:30:43.960 --> 00:30:47.600
basically think of it as like a giant

00:30:45.760 --> 00:30:49.400
filter that's filtering down to the rest

00:30:47.600 --> 00:30:52.680
of the company. And everything across

00:30:49.400 --> 00:30:55.960
these five floors builds towards one

00:30:52.680 --> 00:30:58.800
shift, which again is all in this book,

00:30:55.960 --> 00:31:00.400
Owner or Beyond. So, a few years ago,

00:30:58.800 --> 00:31:02.240
you know, my number two, he actually

00:31:00.400 --> 00:31:04.040
quit over the phone. Uh and he was like

00:31:02.240 --> 00:31:05.720
I think the third key person to leave in

00:31:04.040 --> 00:31:07.426
a month. And I remember like very

00:31:05.720 --> 00:31:09.560
clearly I put my head on the desk and

00:31:07.426 --> 00:31:10.720
[music] finally saw it. I like finally

00:31:09.560 --> 00:31:11.840
saw the truth that I didn't want to

00:31:10.720 --> 00:31:13.440
hear, which was I wasn't running the

00:31:11.840 --> 00:31:15.960
business. I was the business. [music]

00:31:13.440 --> 00:31:18.080
And, you know, every important decision

00:31:15.960 --> 00:31:20.400
was in my head. And so, when this one

00:31:18.080 --> 00:31:21.800
person was leaving, um it could crater

00:31:20.400 --> 00:31:24.560
everything. And the question that turned

00:31:21.800 --> 00:31:26.960
it around was simple. Okay, what system

00:31:24.560 --> 00:31:28.560
needs to exist so it doesn't matter who

00:31:26.960 --> 00:31:30.040
leaves? And that's why I wrote this

00:31:28.560 --> 00:31:32.000
book. I started it that many years ago

00:31:30.040 --> 00:31:34.440
and I wrote Owner or Beyond because this

00:31:32.000 --> 00:31:36.440
is the playbook of the shift for buying

00:31:34.440 --> 00:31:37.840
back your freedom even from the baby

00:31:36.440 --> 00:31:40.800
that you've created, the business that

00:31:37.840 --> 00:31:42.600
you've built. And this is the future.

00:31:40.800 --> 00:31:44.720
So, the question to answer here is which

00:31:42.600 --> 00:31:46.400
floor are you on? Most people are going

00:31:44.720 --> 00:31:48.880
to spend their entire careers on one

00:31:46.400 --> 00:31:51.080
floor. And [music] that is because you

00:31:48.880 --> 00:31:52.800
aren't yet a leader. And remember,

00:31:51.080 --> 00:31:54.080
leadership isn't a personality you're

00:31:52.800 --> 00:31:55.960
born with. It's really just a set of

00:31:54.080 --> 00:31:58.000
skills. And you just watched the ones

00:31:55.960 --> 00:31:59.320
for every level. So, be honest about

00:31:58.000 --> 00:32:01.440
